    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f56a6421-2249-554b-8505-2b2f5f4e6b85",
      ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-5 &=3y \\\\ 24+y &=4x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y &=5 \\\\ -4x+y &=-24\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations: \n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -24\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
